1.	Synchronized methods lock all of the buckets on regular
	collections, which slows down performance. This happens 
	because multiple threads are trying to get the same lock 
	simultaneously.
	
2.	You would choose a CopyOnWriteArrayList when you have
	a program that is not weiting to the array list a lot,
	and mostly performs reads.You use 
	Collections.synchronizedList() when a program is writing 
	to the list a lot. Using CopyOnWriteArrayList for a program
	with a lot of writes slows down performance.
	
3.	You dont use Tree type arrays for concurrent programming
	as they are multi-threaded. This leads to race situations
	because multiple threads are trying to write concurrently.
	
4.	ConcurrentHashMap.compute() is used to turn a get-modify-put
	operation into an atomic one. An atomic operation cannot be
	interrupted by other threads, so it is garunteed to complete.
	